# NOTICE

Rust-nps is an independent Rust implementation that is wire-compatible with
the legacy NPS bridge protocol.

It gratefully acknowledges **ehang-io/nps** (https://github.com/ehang-io/nps),
licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. That project inspired this
work and served as a behavioural reference for interoperability.

No source code from ehang-io/nps is included in this repository. The original
Go sources are kept outside the build tree (see `.gitignore`, `/resources/`),
are never compiled into the shipped binaries, and are used only as a protocol
reference.

Protocol facts — frame layouts, handshake byte sequences, multiplexing window
arithmetic and connection state machines — are functional specifications rather
than copyrightable expression. All Rust code in this repository was written
independently against those specifications and against black-box behaviour of
real clients and servers.

